Kept so this directory always exists in the build context.

The Dockerfile runs COPY public ./public, and a COPY of a source directory that
does not exist fails the build outright. There is no glob form of COPY that
tolerates a total miss, and a RUN mkdir before the COPY would create the
destination but not the source, so an empty file here is what makes the image
build whether or not anything has been committed to public/ yet.

This file is never served: static.js answers only .html, .css, .js, .png and
.svg, and an unrecognised extension is a miss rather than an octet-stream
answer, so a request for /.gitkeep is a JSON 404 like any other unknown path.